 \input{language_scope.tex}
 Empty TEST candidates enter only through HF fallback, giving $f(\emptyset)=(0,0,0,0)$ and centered score $\beta_F^\top x_i(\emptyset)=-\beta_F^\top f(b_i)$. Under signs $(+,+,-,-)$, the margin $-\beta_F^\top f(y)>0$ favors emptiness when $a,p\le0$, $t>0$ and $r\ge0$, even at $r=0$. This ranks candidates rather than assigning transcript probabilities. Reverting all 18 empty acceptances in 11 CV27 recordings to B retains 91.52\% of gain, or 2.10\,pp at 31.88\% WER. The counts suggest hallucination suppression~\cite{baranski2025nonspeech}, but acoustic attribution requires silence labels (Table~\ref{tab:language}). \mbox{H4+$e$ adds} $e(y)=\mathbf1\{y=\emptyset\}$ on H4's DEV folds and grid. With one or two DEV empties per checkpoint, it matches H4's rounded 31.52\% WER and retains all 18 acceptances.
